{"title":"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A figure is constructed from unit cubes. Each cube shares at least one face with another cube. What is the minimum number of cubes needed to build a figure with the front and side views shown?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d30f2f3ae60f8b661b55b5a6167693d0ecc30b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); path p=unitsquare; draw(p^^shift(0,1)*p^^shift(1,0)*p); draw(shift(4,0)*p^^shift(5,0)*p^^shift(5,1)*p); label(&quot;FRONT&quot;, (1,0), S); label(&quot;SIDE&quot;, (5,0), S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"108\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/08479664832994dea9abbe888015464b0221bbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to minimize the amount of cubes needed, we must match up as many squares of our given figures with each other to make different sides of the same cube.  One example of the solution with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f03028c2292cd337ee145bd8db85ebe2afe59d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> cubes. Notice the corner cube cannot be removed for a figure of 3 cubes because at least one face of a cube must be touching another face.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dcf40aa4a89c2511ba153f0441f53298e075bef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); real r=0.5; currentprojection=orthographic(3/4,8/15,7/15); draw(unitcube, white, thick(), nolight); draw(shift(1,-1,0)*unitcube, white, thick(), nolight); draw(shift(1,0,0)*unitcube, white, thick(), nolight); draw(shift(1,0,1)*unitcube, white, thick(), nolight);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eDpxHt1LL7g\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eDpxHt1LL7g</a>\n</p><p>~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8\">2003 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.ph